# Database Design

Database design means deciding how the app data should be organized.

For a production RAG app, we need more than PDF files.

We need structured records for users, documents, chunks, and chats.

## Main Tables Or Collections

Simple database structure:

```text
users
teams
team_members
team_invites
rag_documents
rag_chunks
document_versions
activity_logs
conversations
messages
usage_logs
```

## Users

Stores who can use the app.

Example:

```js
{
  id: "user_001",
  name: "Admin User",
  email: "admin@example.com",
  role: "admin",
  createdAt: "2026-05-24"
}
```

## Documents

Stores uploaded or indexed files.

Example:

```js
{
  id: "doc_001",
  ownerId: "user_001",
  teamId: "team_001",
  fileName: "company-x-branch-morocco.pdf",
  displayName: "Morocco branch policy",
  accessLevel: "team",
  status: "indexed",
  version: 2,
  chunkCount: 135,
  storedPath: "uploads/..."
}
```

## Teams

Stores shared workspaces for users.

Example:

```js
{
  id: "team_001",
  ownerId: "user_001",
  name: "HR Knowledge Team"
}
```

## Team Members

Stores team access and team role.

Example:

```js
{
  teamId: "team_001",
  userId: "user_002",
  role: "member"
}
```

Supported roles:

```text
owner
admin
member
```

## Team Invitations

Stores pending invitations for emails that may not have accounts yet.

Example:

```js
{
  teamId: "team_001",
  email: "new.member@example.com",
  role: "member",
  status: "pending"
}
```

## Chunks

Stores document pieces.

Example:

```js
{
  id: "chunk_001",
  documentId: "doc_001",
  page: 6,
  chunkIndex: 40,
  text: "CX-MA-001 - Amina Morrison...",
  metadata: {
    source: "company x branch morocco"
  }
}
```

## Conversations

Stores chat sessions.

Example:

```js
{
  id: "conv_001",
  userId: "user_001",
  title: "Morocco branch questions",
  createdAt: "2026-05-24"
}
```

## Messages

Stores user and assistant messages.

Example:

```js
{
  id: "msg_001",
  conversationId: "conv_001",
  role: "user",
  content: "What is the salary of CX-MA-001?"
}
```

## Usage Logs

Stores token usage and cost tracking.

Example:

```js
{
  id: "usage_001",
  conversationId: "conv_001",
  promptTokens: 3201,
  completionTokens: 262,
  totalTokens: 3463
}
```

## Document Versions

Stores each indexed or re-indexed version.

Example:

```js
{
  documentId: "doc_001",
  version: 2,
  action: "reindexed",
  chunkCount: 140
}
```

## Activity Logs

Stores important actions for documents and teams.

Example:

```js
{
  action: "document.renamed",
  entityType: "document",
  entityId: "doc_001",
  message: "Renamed old name to new name."
}
```

## Simple Presentation Version

```text
Database design organizes users, teams, invites, documents, chunks, versions, activity logs, conversations, and messages. This makes the app easier to manage, audit, and scale.
```
